msgid ""
msgstr ""
"Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8\n"

#: apps/playground/src/app/app.html:10
msgctxt "Small badge beside the product name; labels this page as an interactive demo/sandbox, not a children's playground"
msgid "playground"
msgstr "démo"

#: apps/playground/src/app/app.html:21
msgctxt "Tooltip on a status dot. 'isReady()' is an API name — keep it verbatim. 'gate UI on this' = show the UI only once it is ready; 'flash-of-untranslated-content' is the technical term for untranslated text briefly showing (FOUC)"
msgid "isReady() — gate UI on this to avoid flash-of-untranslated-content"
msgstr "isReady() — conditionner l'affichage de l'interface utilisateur à cet état pour éviter le flash de contenu non traduit"

#: apps/playground/src/app/app.html:29
msgid "ready"
msgstr "prêt"

#: apps/playground/src/app/app.html:29
msgid "loading…"
msgstr "chargement…"

#: apps/playground/src/app/app.html:57
msgctxt "Heading above the sidebar table-of-contents navigation links"
msgid "On this page"
msgstr "Sur cette page"

#: apps/playground/src/app/app.html:87
msgctxt "Hero tagline (marketing register). 'Angular' is the framework name and 'i18n' the abbreviation for internationalization — keep both. 'signal-first' means built around Angular Signals; render the technical sense, not 'first signal'"
msgid "Angular i18n, the signal-first way"
msgstr "i18n Angular, l'approche signal-first"

#: apps/playground/src/app/app.html:94
msgctxt "Hero subheading (marketing prose). Keep the product/tech names verbatim: 'ng-linguo', 'Angular', 'SignalStore', 'HTML', 'i18n'. 'signals'/'store methods' are Angular Signals concepts; 'read translations'/'change the language' describe data access, not literal reading/writing"
msgid "ng-linguo is a complete internationalization (i18n) toolkit for Angular, built on a SignalStore. You read translations as signals, change the language through store methods, and your translators never touch a line of HTML. Use the language switcher above and watch every example on this page update instantly."
msgstr "ng-linguo est une boîte à outils complète d'internationalisation (i18n) pour Angular, basée sur un SignalStore. Vous lisez les traductions comme des signaux, changez la langue via des méthodes de store, et vos traducteurs ne touchent jamais une ligne de HTML. Utilisez le sélecteur de langue ci-dessus et regardez chaque exemple de cette page se mettre à jour instantanément."

#: apps/playground/src/app/app.html:103
msgctxt "Highlight title. Means: the English source text itself is used as the translation lookup key (no separate key names)"
msgid "English is the key"
msgstr "L'anglais est la clé"

#: apps/playground/src/app/app.html:108
msgctxt "Highlight body. 'lookup key' = the value used to find a translation; 'dotted key paths' = names like home.header.title used by other i18n libraries; 'AI model' = an LLM doing the translation"
msgid "Write real sentences in your components — that text is the lookup key. No dotted key paths to invent or keep in sync, and an AI model always sees full, meaningful context."
msgstr "Écrivez de vraies phrases dans vos composants — ce texte est la clé de recherche. Pas de chemins de clés pointés à inventer ou à synchroniser, et un modèle d'IA voit toujours un contexte complet et significatif."

#: apps/playground/src/app/app.html:115
msgctxt "Highlight title: translation files contain plain text only, no HTML markup"
msgid "Translators never see HTML"
msgstr "Les traducteurs ne voient jamais de HTML"

#: apps/playground/src/app/app.html:120
msgctxt "Highlight body. 'Named slots' = the [name] bracket placeholders; 'Cross-site scripting' = the XSS security vulnerability"
msgid "Named slots bind to your own templates, so links and bold text render as real Angular while the file stays plain text. Cross-site scripting is impossible by design."
msgstr "Les slots nommés se lient à vos propres templates, de sorte que les liens et le texte en gras sont rendus comme du vrai Angular tandis que le fichier reste en texte brut. Le cross-site scripting est impossible par conception."

#: apps/playground/src/app/app.html:127
msgctxt "Highlight title: correct grammatical forms (plurals, gender, etc.) in each language"
msgid "Real grammar, every language"
msgstr "Une grammaire réelle, pour chaque langue"

#: apps/playground/src/app/app.html:132
msgctxt "Highlight body. Keep 'ICU MessageFormat 2' verbatim (a standard). 'locale-aware numbers' = numbers formatted per language"
msgid "ICU MessageFormat 2 handles plurals, ordinals, gender, and locale-aware numbers — Polish gets four plural forms, English gets two, from a single message."
msgstr "ICU MessageFormat 2 gère les pluriels, les ordinaux, le genre et les nombres sensibles à la locale — le polonais obtient quatre formes plurielles, l'anglais en obtient deux, à partir d'un seul message."

#: apps/playground/src/app/app.html:139
msgctxt "Highlight title. 'Additive' = re-running the extractor adds to your files without overwriting existing translations"
msgid "Additive extraction"
msgstr "Extraction additive"

#: apps/playground/src/app/app.html:144
msgctxt "Highlight body. 'extractor' = the CLI that scans source for strings; 'catalogs' = the per-language translation files"
msgid "Re-run the extractor any time: new and changed strings merge into your catalogs while every existing translation is kept."
msgstr "Relancez l'extracteur à tout moment : les chaînes nouvelles et modifiées sont fusionnées dans vos catalogues tandis que chaque traduction existante est conservée."

#: apps/playground/src/app/app.html:151
msgctxt "Highlight title: translating the app using an AI / LLM"
msgid "Translate with AI"
msgstr "Traduire avec l'IA"

#: apps/playground/src/app/app.html:156
msgctxt "Highlight body. 'guided command-line tool' = the interactive CLI; 'chat model' = an LLM such as ChatGPT/Gemini/Claude"
msgid "A guided command-line tool copies a prompt for any chat model, or calls your own AI provider. Adding a whole new language is a single command."
msgstr "Un outil en ligne de commande guidé copie une invite pour n'importe quel modèle de chat, ou appelle votre propre fournisseur d'IA. Ajouter une toute nouvelle langue est une seule commande."

#: apps/playground/src/app/app.html:163
msgctxt "Highlight title. Keep 'SSR' (server-side rendering) and 'tree-shakeable' (unused code is dropped from the bundle); 'Zoneless' = works without Angular's zone.js"
msgid "Zoneless, SSR-safe, tree-shakeable"
msgstr "Sans zone, compatible SSR, tree-shakeable"

#: apps/playground/src/app/app.html:168
msgctxt "Highlight body. Keep 'signals' (Angular Signals) and 'zone.js' (Angular library name) verbatim; 'renders on the server' = supports server-side rendering"
msgid "Reactivity is signals all the way down. No zone.js, it renders on the server, and optional features ship only when you import them."
msgstr "La réactivité est basée sur les signaux de bout en bout. Pas de zone.js, il est rendu côté serveur, et les fonctionnalités optionnelles ne sont livrées que lorsque vous les importez."

#: apps/playground/src/app/app.html:180
msgctxt "Section-group label for the first group of examples: installing the library and the three basic ways to translate (the t pipe, the [t] directive, and injectTranslate)"
msgid "Getting started"
msgstr "Démarrage rapide"

#: apps/playground/src/app/app.html:188
msgctxt "Section heading: initial setup / installation of the library"
msgid "Setup"
msgstr "Configuration"

#: apps/playground/src/app/app.html:195
msgctxt "Card title. 'translation store' = the ng-linguo SignalStore that holds translations (a noun)"
msgid "Set up the translation store"
msgstr "Configurer le store de traduction"

#: apps/playground/src/app/app.html:199
msgctxt "Card body (developer-docs tone, step-by-step). Keep API names verbatim: provideTranslate(), restoreLang(), injectTranslate(). 'persisted → browser → default' is the order restoreLang() chooses the startup language in; 'keyed by' = uses as the lookup key; 'CLI' = the command-line tool"
msgid "Three steps to a translated app: (1) register the store with provideTranslate() — it never fetches on its own; (2) load a language at startup with restoreLang(), which picks persisted → browser → default; (3) translate with the pipe, directive, or injectTranslate(). Translation files are plain JSON keyed by the original English text — generate them with the CLI shown under Tooling & workflow below."
msgstr "Trois étapes pour une application traduite : (1) enregistrez le store avec provideTranslate() — il ne récupère jamais de lui-même ; (2) chargez une langue au démarrage avec restoreLang(), qui choisit persistant → navigateur → par défaut ; (3) traduisez avec le pipe, la directive ou injectTranslate(). Les fichiers de traduction sont des JSON simples indexés par le texte anglais original — générez-les avec l'outil en ligne de commande (CLI) présenté dans la section Outils et flux de travail ci-dessous."

#: apps/playground/src/app/app.html:209
msgctxt "Section heading. 'pipe' is the Angular template-pipe concept — keep the technical term; [code] wraps the code symbol 't'"
msgid "The [code]t[/code] pipe"
msgstr "Le pipe [code]t[/code]"

#: apps/playground/src/app/app.html:220
msgctxt "Card title. 'template' = the Angular HTML template"
msgid "Translate in the template"
msgstr "Traduire dans le template"

#: apps/playground/src/app/app.html:223
msgctxt "Card body. 'lookup key' = the value used to find a translation; the point is that the original English is both what you write and the key. 'never empty' = no blank UI"
msgid "Write the English text straight into your template — that text is the lookup key. If a translation is missing, the pipe shows the English instead, so the screen is never empty."
msgstr "Écrivez le texte anglais directement dans votre template — ce texte est la clé de recherche. Si une traduction est manquante, le pipe affiche l'anglais à la place, de sorte que l'écran n'est jamais vide."

#: apps/playground/src/app/app.html:228
#: apps/playground/src/app/app.html:262
msgid "Welcome back!"
msgstr "Bon retour !"

#: apps/playground/src/app/app.html:243
msgctxt "Section heading. 'directive' is the Angular directive concept — keep the technical term; [code] wraps the code symbol '[t]'"
msgid "The [code][[t][/code] directive"
msgstr "La directive [code][[t][/code]"

#: apps/playground/src/app/app.html:254
msgctxt "Card title. 'element' = an HTML / DOM element"
msgid "Translate an element"
msgstr "Traduire un élément"

#: apps/playground/src/app/app.html:257
msgctxt "Card body. 'signals' = Angular Signals; 'translation file' = the JSON dictionary; 'directive' = the Angular [t] directive; 'RxJS subscriptions to manage' = manual subscribe/unsubscribe bookkeeping"
msgid "Put the text on the element itself. The directive watches the store's signals for you, so when a translation file finishes loading the element updates on its own — no RxJS subscriptions to manage."
msgstr "Placez le texte directement sur l'élément. La directive surveille les signaux du store pour vous, de sorte que lorsqu'un fichier de traduction a fini de charger, l'élément se met à jour de lui-même — aucune souscription RxJS à gérer."

#: apps/playground/src/app/app.html:273
msgctxt "Card title. 'TypeScript' is the programming language name — keep verbatim"
msgid "Translate in TypeScript"
msgstr "Traduire en TypeScript"

#: apps/playground/src/app/app.html:276
msgctxt "Card body. 'the pipe' = the Angular t pipe; 'TypeScript' = component class code; keep computed() verbatim; 'parameters' = the ICU placeholder values; 'updates automatically' = stays reactive"
msgid "The pipe's equivalent for TypeScript. Call it inside a computed() and the result updates automatically whenever your parameters or the active language change."
msgstr "L'équivalent du pipe pour TypeScript. Appelez-le à l'intérieur d'un computed() et le résultat se met à jour automatiquement chaque fois que vos paramètres ou la langue active changent."

#: apps/playground/src/app/app.html:299
msgctxt "Section-group label: examples that rely on ICU MessageFormat — plurals, ordinals, gender selection, and number formatting"
msgid "Plurals & formatting"
msgstr "Pluriels et formatage"

#: apps/playground/src/app/app.html:307
msgctxt "Section heading: grammatical plural forms (one file / many files)"
msgid "Plurals"
msgstr "Pluriels"

#: apps/playground/src/app/app.html:314
msgctxt "Card title. 'Counting plurals' = cardinal forms (1 file / 2 files), as opposed to ordinals like 1st/2nd"
msgid "Counting plurals across languages"
msgstr "Comptage des pluriels selon les langues"

#: apps/playground/src/app/app.html:318
msgctxt "Card body. one/few/many/other are CLDR plural-category names — keep them in English; 'count' is a variable name (keep); the point is that different languages need a different number of plural forms"
msgid "English has two forms (one/other); Polish has four (one/few/many/other). You can also give an exact '0' form when 'No new messages' reads better than '0 messages'. Step count through 1, 2, 5, 22 in Polish to watch the form change."
msgstr "L'anglais a deux formes (one/other) ; le polonais en a quatre (one/few/many/other). Vous pouvez également donner une forme exacte pour '0' lorsque 'Aucun nouveau message' est plus clair que '0 messages'. Faites varier le nombre à 1, 2, 5, 22 en polonais pour observer le changement de forme."

#: apps/playground/src/app/app.html:354
msgctxt "Section heading: ordinal numbers (1st, 2nd, 3rd …), not cardinal counts"
msgid "Ordinals"
msgstr "Ordinaux"

#: apps/playground/src/app/app.html:361
msgctxt "Card title. 'Ordinal numbers' = ranking forms; keep the 1st/2nd/3rd examples as English ordinal suffixes"
msgid "Ordinal numbers (1st, 2nd, 3rd …)"
msgstr "Nombres ordinaux (1er, 2e, 3e…)"

#: apps/playground/src/app/app.html:365
msgctxt "Card body. st/nd/rd/th are the English ordinal suffixes; one/two/few/other are CLDR category names (keep in English); EN/PL/DE meaning English/Polish/German; '{n}.' shows the number followed by a period"
msgid "English picks st/nd/rd/th depending on the number (one/two/few/other); Polish and German just add a period, like '{n}.'."
msgstr "L'anglais utilise st/nd/rd/th selon le nombre (one/two/few/other) ; le polonais et l'allemand ajoutent simplement un point, comme '{n}.'."

#: apps/playground/src/app/app.html:402
msgctxt "Section heading. 'select' is the ICU MessageFormat 'select' construct (pick a variant by gender) — not a dropdown and not the verb 'to select'"
msgid "Gender select"
msgstr "Sélection par genre"

#: apps/playground/src/app/app.html:409
msgctxt "Card title. This demonstrates the ICU 'select' construct: choosing a different sentence depending on a value (here, gender)"
msgid "Pick the wording by gender"
msgstr "Choisir la formulation par genre"

#: apps/playground/src/app/app.html:413
msgctxt "Card body. 'pronoun' = she/he/they; 'verb ending' = a verb form that changes with gender (as in Polish); 'matches on count and gender at the same time' = one message that depends on two values at once"
msgid "English changes the pronoun (she/he/they); Polish changes the verb ending. The second line matches on count and gender at the same time — and every combination can read differently from one language to the next."
msgstr "L'anglais change le pronom (she/he/they) ; le polonais change la terminaison du verbe. La deuxième ligne correspond au nombre et au genre en même temps — et chaque combinaison peut se lire différemment d'une langue à l'autre."

#: apps/playground/src/app/app.html:436
msgctxt "Section heading: locale-aware number formatting (digit-group separators)"
msgid "Number formatting"
msgstr "Formatage des nombres"

#: apps/playground/src/app/app.html:443
msgctxt "Card title. 'Digit grouping' = the separators inside large numbers (1,000 vs 1.000 vs 1 000), which differ by language"
msgid "Digit grouping per language"
msgstr "Regroupement des chiffres par langue"

#: apps/playground/src/app/app.html:447
msgctxt "Card body. ':number' is an ICU formatter token (keep verbatim); en/de/pl meaning English/German/Polish; the figures show how each language groups thousands"
msgid "The :number formatter groups digits the way each language expects: en 1,234,567 · de 1.234.567 · pl 1 234 567."
msgstr "Le formateur :number regroupe les chiffres comme chaque langue l'attend : en 1,234,567 · de 1.234.567 · pl 1 234 567."

#: apps/playground/src/app/app.html:460
msgctxt "Section-group label: more advanced translation features — disambiguating identical words by context, and rich text with slot tags"
msgid "Advanced messages"
msgstr "Messages avancés"

#: apps/playground/src/app/app.html:468
msgctxt "Section heading. 'Context' = the translation disambiguation feature (gettext msgctxt); 'homonyms' = words spelled the same but meaning different things"
msgid "Context (homonyms)"
msgstr "Contexte (homonymes)"

#: apps/playground/src/app/app.html:475
msgctxt "Card title about homonyms / disambiguation"
msgid "Same word, different meaning"
msgstr "Même mot, sens différent"

#: apps/playground/src/app/app.html:478
msgctxt "Card body. 'context' is the ng-linguo option name (keep verbatim); 'key' = lookup key; 'msgctxt' is the gettext technical term (keep); the same English word can map to different translations"
msgid "A context label becomes part of the key (gettext calls it msgctxt) and also tells the translator which meaning you mean. Switch to Polish to see each one translated differently."
msgstr "Une étiquette de contexte fait partie de la clé (gettext l'appelle msgctxt) et indique également au traducteur le sens que vous voulez donner. Passez au polonais pour voir chaque traduction différente."

#: apps/playground/src/app/app.html:485
msgctxt "audio player"
msgid "Play"
msgstr "Lecture"

#: apps/playground/src/app/app.html:485
msgctxt "game"
msgid "Play"
msgstr "Jouer"

#: apps/playground/src/app/app.html:489
msgctxt "direction"
msgid "Right"
msgstr "Droite"

#: apps/playground/src/app/app.html:489
msgctxt "correct"
msgid "Right"
msgstr "Juste"

#: apps/playground/src/app/app.html:493
msgctxt "sequence"
msgid "Order"
msgstr "Ordre"

#: apps/playground/src/app/app.html:493
msgctxt "purchase"
msgid "Order"
msgstr "Commande"

#: apps/playground/src/app/app.html:497
msgctxt "no cost"
msgid "Free"
msgstr "Gratuit"

#: apps/playground/src/app/app.html:497
msgctxt "available"
msgid "Free"
msgstr "Libre"

#: apps/playground/src/app/app.html:506
msgctxt "Section heading. 'Rich text' = text with links/emphasis; 'slot tags' = the [name] bracket placeholders ng-linguo uses in translations"
msgid "Rich text (slot tags)"
msgstr "Texte enrichi (balises de slot)"

#: apps/playground/src/app/app.html:513
msgctxt "Card title. The point: links and styled text appear in the UI, but the translation files stay plain text with no HTML"
msgid "Links and bold text — with no HTML in your translation files"
msgstr "Liens et texte en gras — sans HTML dans vos fichiers de traduction"

#: apps/playground/src/app/app.html:517
msgctxt "Card body. 'named slots' = the [name] bracket placeholders; keep 'ng-template tFor' verbatim; 'real bracket' = a literal [ character; 'XSS' is the web-security term (keep). [[name]…[[/name] is escaped so it shows as the literal text [name]…[/name] — keep the doubled brackets"
msgid "Translators only ever see named slots like [[name]…[[/name] — never HTML tags. You bind each slot to your own ng-template tFor, so you decide what it renders as: a link, bold text, anything. Need a real bracket in your text? Type the opening one twice. Translated text is never inserted as HTML, so cross-site scripting (XSS) is impossible by design."
msgstr "Les traducteurs ne voient que des slots nommés comme [[name]…[[/name] — jamais de balises HTML. Vous liez chaque slot à votre propre ng-template tFor, vous décidez donc de ce qu'il rend : un lien, du texte en gras, n'importe quoi. Besoin d'un vrai crochet dans votre texte ? Tapez le crochet ouvrant deux fois. Le texte traduit n'est jamais inséré comme du HTML, donc le cross-site scripting (XSS) est impossible par conception."

#: apps/playground/src/app/app.html:523
msgctxt "Onboarding hint. [docs] wraps a link to the documentation — translate the wrapped word too and keep the [docs] tags around it"
msgid "Read the [docs]documentation[/docs] to get started"
msgstr "Lisez la [docs]documentation[/docs] pour commencer"

#: apps/playground/src/app/app.html:531
msgctxt "Consent line shown before sign-up. [terms] wraps a link; 'Terms of Service' is the standard name of the legal agreement — use the conventional target-language equivalent"
msgid "By continuing you agree to our [terms]Terms of Service[/terms]"
msgstr "En continuant, vous acceptez nos [terms]Conditions d'utilisation[/terms]"

#: apps/playground/src/app/app.html:539
msgctxt "Warning before a destructive, irreversible action. [warn] wraps the emphasized lead word 'Warning:'"
msgid "[warn]Warning:[/warn] this action cannot be undone"
msgstr "[warn]Attention :[/warn] cette action est irréversible"

#: apps/playground/src/app/app.html:548
msgctxt "Demo of ng-linguo's slot syntax and its bracket escape. 'Escaped' is the programming sense (made literal via the [[ escape), not fleeing; 'stays literal' = shown as plain text; 'slot' = a fillable [name] region. [[b]bold[[/b] is escaped literal text, [b]this[/b] is a real slot — keep both forms exactly"
msgid "Escaped [[b]bold[[/b] stays literal — [b]this[/b] is a slot"
msgstr "[[b]bold[[/b] échappé reste littéral — [b]ceci[/b] est un slot"

#: apps/playground/src/app/app.html:559
msgctxt "Consent line with a nested slot. [link] wraps a link to the Terms; [b] emphasizes a word inside it. 'Terms and Conditions' is the standard legal-document name — use the conventional target-language equivalent"
msgid "Agree to our [link]Terms and [b]Conditions[/b][/link]"
msgstr "Acceptez nos [link]Conditions [b]Générales[/b][/link]"

#: apps/playground/src/app/app.html:578
msgctxt "Section-group label: the surrounding workflow — the ESLint setup and the extract/translate/compile pipeline"
msgid "Tooling & workflow"
msgstr "Outils et flux de travail"

#: apps/playground/src/app/app.html:586
msgctxt "Section heading. 'ESLint' is a tool name — keep verbatim; 'a11y' is the numeronym for accessibility (keep, or use the target word for accessibility)"
msgid "ESLint & a11y"
msgstr "ESLint et a11y"

#: apps/playground/src/app/app.html:593
msgctxt "Card title (colloquial). 'accessibility linter' = the ESLint a11y rule; 'keep it happy' = satisfy the rule; '[t]' is a code symbol (keep); 'empty elements' = elements with no text written in the HTML"
msgid "Keep the accessibility linter happy with empty [t] elements"
msgstr "Satisfaire le linter d'accessibilité avec des éléments [t] vides"

#: apps/playground/src/app/app.html:597
msgctxt "Card body. Keep verbatim: @angular-eslint/template/elements-content, [t]. 'markup' = the HTML you write; 'fallback' = text shown before translations load; 'the hero' = the large heading at the top of the page"
msgid "Angular's accessibility rule @angular-eslint/template/elements-content warns about empty headings, links, and buttons. A [t] element gets its text at runtime, so you can leave the markup empty — every heading on this page is an empty [t] element, and only the hero keeps its text as a fallback shown before translations load."
msgstr "La règle d'accessibilité d'Angular @angular-eslint/template/elements-content avertit des titres, liens et boutons vides. Un élément [t] obtient son texte à l'exécution, vous pouvez donc laisser le balisage vide — chaque titre de cette page est un élément [t] vide, et seul le titre principal conserve son texte comme solution de repli affichée avant le chargement des traductions."

#: apps/playground/src/app/app.html:607
msgctxt "Section heading: the build-time CLI pipeline that turns source strings into translated files (extract, translate, compile)"
msgid "Translation workflow"
msgstr "Flux de travail de traduction"

#: apps/playground/src/app/app.html:614
msgctxt "Card title. 'English source' = the original strings; 'translated files' = the per-language .po/.json files"
msgid "From English source to translated files"
msgstr "De la source anglaise aux fichiers traduits"

#: apps/playground/src/app/app.html:618
msgctxt "Card body. Keep verbatim: extract CLI, gettext, .po, JSON, ng-linguo, SDK, API key, translator, CI. 'additive' = re-running adds without overwriting; 'guided menu' = the interactive CLI; 'chat model' = an LLM such as ChatGPT/Gemini/Claude; 'merges the reply' = applies the model's response back into the files"
msgid "The extract CLI scans your source, keeps the strings in standard gettext .po files, and compiles them to the JSON the app loads. Re-running it is additive — new strings merge in, existing translations stay. Run it with no command for a guided menu, or as plain commands in CI. To translate, copy a ready-made prompt into any chat model, or point the translator option at a small module that calls your own AI provider — ng-linguo writes the prompt and merges the reply, and your SDK and API key never leave your machine."
msgstr "L'outil en ligne de commande (CLI) d'extraction analyse votre code source, conserve les chaînes dans des fichiers .po gettext standard et les compile en JSON que l'application charge. Le relancer est additif — les nouvelles chaînes sont fusionnées, les traductions existantes sont conservées. Exécutez-le sans commande pour un menu guidé, ou comme de simples commandes en CI. Pour traduire, copiez une invite prête à l'emploi dans n'importe quel modèle de chat, ou pointez l'option de traducteur vers un petit module qui appelle votre propre fournisseur d'IA — ng-linguo écrit l'invite et fusionne la réponse, et votre SDK et clé API ne quittent jamais votre machine."

#: apps/playground/src/app/app.html:629
msgctxt "Page footer. 'ng-linguo' is the product name (keep verbatim); 'living documentation' = documentation that is also a working demo"
msgid "Built with ng-linguo · this playground is also living documentation."
msgstr "Construit avec ng-linguo · ce bac à sable est aussi une documentation vivante."

#: apps/playground/src/app/app.ts:59
msgid "Getting started"
msgstr "Démarrage rapide"

#: apps/playground/src/app/app.ts:61
msgid "Setup"
msgstr "Configuration"

#: apps/playground/src/app/app.ts:62
msgid "The t pipe"
msgstr "Le pipe t"

#: apps/playground/src/app/app.ts:63
msgid "The [t] directive"
msgstr "La directive [t]"

#: apps/playground/src/app/app.ts:69
msgid "Plurals & formatting"
msgstr "Pluriels et formatage"

#: apps/playground/src/app/app.ts:71
msgid "Plurals"
msgstr "Pluriels"

#: apps/playground/src/app/app.ts:72
msgid "Ordinals"
msgstr "Ordinaux"

#: apps/playground/src/app/app.ts:73
